    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1937899684913180866",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1937899684913180866",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1937899684913180866",
      "text": "[4:40PM] #Okota_Isolo #TrafficUpdate \n\nCele to Pako, along with the return journey, is currently clear. Ago Palace Road is also reporting good traffic conditions for both inbound and outbound travel, including the Apple Junction area.\n\n Motorists using Nwachukwu Drive to connect to Cele can expect unimpeded journeys in both directions. Similarly, the Cele-linked bridge towards Ijesha is currently experiencing good traffic flow for both inbound and outbound commuters.\n\n Within Ire Akari, the stretch connecting to Osolo Road is also clear in both directions. Along Ibeh Road Apata, the route from Transformer Junction to Ilasa under the bridge service lane is currently good for both inbound and outbound traffic. \n\nOke Afa, specifically the stretch leading towards the Lasutech roundabout, is also reporting smooth traffic in both directions. Daleko bridge inbound to Palm Avenue Junction is currently clear for travel in both directions. \n\nFinally, Five Stars, including both the main carriage ways and service lanes towards Ijesha express, is currently experiencing good traffic flow with no reported impediments at present.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
